{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966810,"nonce":"Il+t6qQwC/1+U/SnJhgJvN+43YE=","title":"zyntax translate_closure seeds var_types but not var_typed_ast_types for lambda params —","message":"`translate_closure` (compiler/src/ssa.rs) inserts each lambda param into `self.var_types` (HIR-side, e.g. `Ptr(I8)` for strings) but pre-fix did NOT insert into `self.var_typed_ast_types` (TypedAst-side `Type::Primitive(String)`).\n\nDownstream resolvers that need the TypedAst-side type — `.field` / `.method()` dispatch, match-arm string-eq routing in lower_match_blocks, `__fstring_format__` desugaring — read `var_typed_ast_types` and fall back to `Type::Any`. `Type::Any` gets treated as Int (i32/i64) by every code path that branches on operand type. So a string lambda param like `|state: string|` arrives in the body as the right pointer in HIR but the TypedAst layer thinks it's an integer.\n\nSymptom: `f\"got={state}\"` desugars to `__fstring_format__(state)` which the action interpreter routes to `$Blinc$format_int` (i32 only) — outputs the pointer truncated to i32 as a decimal integer. Match arms comparing `state == \"literal\"` fall back to integer Eq (pointer-as-i64 vs string-literal-pointer-as-i64) which never matches.\n\n**Why:** Outer captures already had `var_typed_ast_types` mirroring (see comment in translate_closure around line 8680: \"ALSO mirror the TypedAST-side type ...\"). Lambda params were the missing case. The outer-capture comment even called out the same Blinc-side symptom (`count.set(...)` failing with \"Cannot access fields on non-struct type: Any\").\n\n**How to apply:** Fixed in zyntax `ac32934e0ce4651048a0ea8b3733283d379d1577` — same commit as [[gotcha-zyntax-closure-body-control-flow]]. When introducing new lambda-param plumbing (e.g. multi-arg closures, generic params), mirror `var_types.insert(...)` with `var_typed_ast_types.insert(param.name, typed_ty.clone())` whenever `param.ty.as_ref()` is `Some`.","files":null}]}